        {
          "title": "Efficient Streaming Audio-Visual Target Speaker Extraction for Real-World Acoustic Scenes",
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.32749",
          "source": "HuggingFace Papers",
          "date": "2026-10-29T00:00:00+00:00",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "arxiv_top",
          "raw_content": "Streaming audio-visual target speaker extraction (AVTSE) is essential for latency-sensitive applications. However, current causal systems face two coupled gaps. First, standard benchmarks fix the number of speakers at two and ignore the near-/far-field interference, reverberation, and sudden noise of real scenes. Second, high-performance causal architectures are too heavy for edge deployment. Lightweight alternatives try to reclaim capacity by repeatedly invoking a small separator, which offsets the savings. To address the first gap, we release RealSSA, a realistic AVTSE benchmark consisting of RealSSA-Sim and RealSSA-Real. RealSSA-Sim provides controllable simulated scenes with 1--5 dynamic near-field interfering speakers; scenes with far-field interference additionally include 10--15 far-field interfering speakers. RealSSA-Real provides a held-out real-recorded evaluation set. To addre",
          "organization": "",
          "arxiv_id": "2610.32749",
          "link_verified": true,
          "focus_match": [],
          "priority_hint": 7,
          "title_zh": "",
          "summary": "",
          "keywords": [
